KNOWNBUG itanium-abi
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ empty base: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ at offset 0: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ storing the member writes nothing: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ member of a non-empty base: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
static assertion failed
--
H was not empty (is_empty, and as a base), and the member of a base kept
its offset within the base: T was 8 bytes with H at offset 4, its end, so
copying h.e read past the end of t.
Tagged itanium-abi: Visual Studio ignores [[no_unique_address]] (it has
[[msvc::no_unique_address]]), which [intro.object]/8 permits, and so does
cbmc's Visual Studio mode.
